  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "The equations \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) and \\(bx - 10 = -2\\) have the same solution for \\(x.\\) What is the value of \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-8\\)",
    "B": "\\(-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First find the shared value of \\(x\\) using the equation that contains no \\(b\\). Subtracting \\(7\\) from both sides of \\(2x+7=3\\) gives \\(2x=-4\\), so \\(x=-2\\).\n\nThis same value must satisfy the second equation. Substituting it, then adding \\(10\\) to both sides and dividing by \\(-2\\), gives\n\\[\n-2b-10=-2,\\qquad -2b=8,\\qquad b=-4.\n\\]\nThus \\(b=\\boxed{-4}\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
